# Datums on a solid (an extension): a plate whose corner a fillet
# rounds, its fillet's face named corner and its bottom base
# (testdata/datums/rounded.tlspr, examples/scripts/datums_solid), is
# linked twice into an empty model. Edit > Datums lists both links'
# names; [mate] on the first's corner, then the second's, offers the
# mates of two names, and [concentric] puts the second's corner on the
# first's axis; the second link keeps 2 degrees of freedom, turning about
# and sliding along the axis.
file $testdata/datums/host.tlspr
menu File|Open...
file $testdata/datums/rounded.tlspr
menu Assembly|Link / Assemble...
file $testdata/datums/rounded.tlspr
menu Assembly|Link / Assemble...
menu Edit|Datums...
tw
twmove 361 180
twdown L 361 180
twup L 361 180
twmove 361 250
twdown L 361 250
twup L 361 250
tw
twmove 154 320
twdown L 154 320
twup L 154 320
tw
twmove 28 10
twdown L 28 10
twup L 28 10
tw
